---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { legalCompany, legalMailto } from "../lib/legal";
---

<Legal
  title="Support — Zenguy"
  description="Support and troubleshooting for the Zenguy iOS companion app."
  heading="Zenguy Support"
  eyebrow="iOS companion app"
  effective="1 September 2026"
>
  <p>
    Zenguy for iOS is a free companion app for people whose organization has
    already provided a Zenguy account, workspace and active access. The iOS app
    does not create accounts or workspaces, sell subscriptions, process
    purchases, or direct people to buy access elsewhere.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact support</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={legalMailto}>{legalCompany.email}</a>. This monitored address
    handles app access, privacy, account deletion, notifications and technical
    problems. Include the app version and build shown at the bottom of
    <strong>Account</strong>, your iOS version, and a description of what
    happened. Never send a password, API key or test secret.
  </p>

  <h2>Sign-in help</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Use the email and password for your existing Zenguy account. There is no
      registration option in the iOS app.
    </li>
    <li>
      Use <strong>Forgot password?</strong> on the sign-in screen if you cannot
      remember the password.
    </li>
    <li>
      If sign-in succeeds but access is unavailable, contact the administrator
      of your organization so they can check your existing workspace access.
      The app deliberately does not show prices or an acquisition path.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Notifications and App Lock</h2>
  <p>
    Push notifications are optional. Enable them from Account and allow
    notifications when iOS asks. If permission was previously denied, open the
    iOS Settings app and select Zenguy. App Lock is also optional; Face ID or
    Touch ID is evaluated by iOS and Zenguy never receives biometric templates.
  </p>

  <h2>Delete an account</h2>
  <p>
    In the signed-in app, open <strong>More → Account → Delete my account</strong>.
    Enter the current password, type DELETE, and confirm. The action revokes
    sessions, removes memberships and deletes every workspace owned by the
    account. It does not require a support request. If you cannot sign in to
    reach the control, email us so we can verify your identity and help with a
    privacy request.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy and optional AI processing</h2>
  <p>
    Read the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> and
    <a href="/privacy-choices/">Privacy choices</a>. OpenAI fallback processing
    is off by default and can only be enabled or revoked by a workspace Owner
    or Admin from <strong>More → AI data sharing</strong>.
  </p>
</Legal>
